START = 1140
EN = [
"Guardians of the Temple",
"Chapter Four · The Fourth Eye",
"The song that Neris, Queen of the Abyss, commanded",
"The sunken city. This is where the song was rising from. Do you hear it? Only two are singing now.",
"There's a slab in the middle of the temple. Looks like a score. The side is crowded with names.",
"We're under water and I can breathe. Is it the song? I won't ask. I'll breathe and be thankful.",
"There were gold coins dropped here. There are rooms behind the slab. The rooms of the ones who quit. Let's go and see.",
"Priests' Cells · The Practice Slate",
"A stone slate leans against the wall in every cell. Eight bars written in a child's hand. Where a note is wrong, there are corrections in an adult's hand. Generation after generation got the same place wrong. The sixth bar.",
"Words in the corner of a slate: \"Seven years old. Night watch from today. If I doze, Mother pinches me.\" Beneath it, in writing from long after: \"Forty years old. From today my daughter takes the night watch. I cannot bring myself to pinch her.\"",
"Oscar the Fisher: From seven years old. …Our Elric was seven the first time he rode in a boat.",
"Priests' Cells · The Tally on the Wall",
"One long wall is covered in tally marks. One mark a day. From one end of the room to the other, from floor to ceiling. The wall ran out and they went on to the ceiling. The ceiling ran out and they went on to the wall of the next cell.",
"Here and there words are wedged between the marks. \"When does the relief come?\" Some three hundred years later: \"The relief does not come. Do not ask.\" Some six hundred years later: \"The children ask what a relief is. I could not explain.\"",
"Oscar the Fisher: So the queen said she'd send a relief. At the start. And didn't. Whether she forgot, or had no one to send.",
"Priests' Cells · Six Empty Bunks",
"Six bunks are empty. The bedding is folded. These were not people who left in a hurry. They folded it and went. On each pillow lies a single grey coin. They did not take them.",
"You pick up a coin. It is cold. The face is worn away; on the back is a crest. The crest is different on every coin. Furnace. Waterway. Cog. Wave. Snowflake. Closed mouth.",
"Oscar the Fisher: They took the money and left the money behind. Means it wasn't money they needed. …These crests. Aren't they the ones they say are carved on the thrones? The six kings'. Whoever struck these coins holds the coin dies of all six kingdoms.",
"Freshly scratched on the wall at the head of the last bunk: \"That person said: 'You may stop. I will put it to sleep another way.' We waited a thousand years for those words. We knew it was a lie, and we took it.\"",
"Pick up the coin",
"Oscar the Fisher: To someone holding back the wish to quit, the most frightening thing isn't a curse. It's the words 'you may stop.'",
"This is where they ate and slept and sang. Forty generations. The cells are small. Smaller than a ship's cabin.",
"There's a slate leaning on the wall. A child's writing.",
"Look at this wall. Tally marks. All of it. They counted the days.",
"Six bunks empty. There's something on the pillows. I'll pick them up.",
"They folded the bedding before they went. People who run don't fold their bedding.",
"Six coins. Every crest different. Let's go up. I'm worried about the two who are left.",
"Deepling Warlocks",
"Elder Guardian of the Temple",
"The First Sounding Stone",
"You stand on a stone worn into the shape of feet. The priest's voice cracks on the sixth bar. You step into that gap and take up the seventh.",
"Your voice is carried down on the water. Far below your feet, something lets out a long breath. The barnacles on the temple pillars all shut at once.",
"Carry on the song",
"The Second Sounding Stone",
"The second stone is worn deeper. Whoever stood here held out the longest. There are knee marks beside the stone. When they could not sing standing, they sang kneeling.",
"Oscar the Fisher: (From the middle stone, off key, loudly) …I'll take the eighth bar! Breathe!",
"For the first time the priest stops singing and draws breath. Hears a lullaby sung by someone else, for the first time in a thousand years. The shoulders shake.",
"The Third Sounding Stone",
"A name is carved on the third stone. Not a priest's. A child's handwriting. \"I want to ride on its back.\" Carved before there was a seal.",
"You sing the last bar. A low sound follows up from below. The beast sings along in its sleep. It knows the eight bars. It has heard them for a thousand years.",
"The priest gestures. Enough. Then unties a shell necklace from their own neck and presses it into Oscar's hand.",
"Oscar the Fisher: You can get the notes wrong. So long as it doesn't break off.",
"Guardians of the Deep Temple",
"(He sings the eight bars low.) …Forgive the wrong notes. It's a fisherman's throat.",
"The Leviathan\nThe beast on whose back the children rode and played. Heard a lullaby for a thousand years.\nForty generations of priests. They tried not to let a single breath break.",
"Red Mushroom",
"Brown Mushroom",
"Bowl",
"The Corner Seat in the Restaurant",
"The priest has avoided the window and sits in the corner. The sunlight is too bright, they say. The backs of the hands are white and swollen from the water. They hold the spoon like someone holding one for the first time.",
"The stew arrives. Steam rises. The priest tries to catch the steam in a hand. When it will not be caught, they laugh. Without sound. Even the way of laughing is the way of under the water.",
"Lorenzo the Restaurant Owner: Eat slowly! It's hot! Ah, you don't know what hot is. Um… it's a good thing that you have to be careful with!",
"\"It is quiet,\" the priest says. The restaurant is noisy. The clatter of plates, Lorenzo's voice, children shouting outside. In the middle of it all the priest says it is quiet. \"There is nothing that must be sung.\"",
"Oscar the Fisher: (From the next seat, with cold soup before him) …I think I know what that means. It was like that the morning after I hung up the lamp. So quiet my ears rang.",
"Lorenzo the Restaurant Owner: Mr. Oscar! Have the hot one today! It's a day for eating with someone who's been waited for! That one there has waited a thousand years. For the relief!",
"Oscar looks at the bowl for a long while. Then he pushes the cold soup aside and takes the hot stew.",
"Sit beside them",
"The Void",
"The Seven Thrones",
"Stone thrones are set in a ring in the round room. A different crest on the back of each. Furnace, waterway, cog, wave, snowflake, closed mouth, flame.",
"On the seat of the furnace, a hammer. On the seat of the waterway, a water jar the size of a palm. On the seat of the cog, a winding key. On the seat of the wave, a shell flute. Each a small model of what its king passed off onto his own kingdom.",
"The seat of the snowflake is smaller than the others. A footrest has been added. The one who sat there could not reach the floor. Scratched into the back with a fingernail: \"I'm scared.\"",
"On the seat of the closed mouth, a lump of sealing wax. It belongs to Velas, King of Silence. Carved on the armrest: \"I will lock the empty seat. So that no one can ask.\"",
"Elder Erwin: Velas was a quiet man. …So it is written. In place of speaking, he covered things over. The eaten names, and the empty seat. A man who believed that what is covered is not there.",
"Endermen of the Void",
"Chapter Four · The Fifth Eye",
"The Empty Throne",
"The seat that Velas, King of Silence, locked",
"…This is the room. Where the thrones stood in a ring. Let us go slowly.",
"Something has been left on each seat. Look at them one by one. Do not touch.",
"Sound lingers long in this room. So everyone spoke softly. …So they say.",
"You have seen the seven seats. There is a niche behind Velas's seat. What he covered over will be there.",
"The Niche · First Canister",
"The sealing wax crumbles under your fingernail. There is the smell of thousand-year-old beeswax. Inside is a thin stone tablet. The letters are neat. The hand of one who takes things down.",
"\"First day. The way to divide the fire was put forward. One whole name must be fed to it. Silence.\" \"Second day. Whose name? Silence.\" \"Third day. The King of Frost spoke of a prisoner. One against.\"",
"Where the name of the one who was against was written, the stone is sunken. It was not dug out. The letters went out by themselves. The stone forgot that name.",
"Break the seal",
"The Niche · Second Canister",
"\"Fourth day. King of the Furnace: I cannot choose from among my people. King of the Waterway: nor can I. Queen of Cogs: let it be calculated. Silence.\"",
"\"Fifth day. No one came. The one taking it down sat alone.\" Below it in another hand, small: \"Only the one whose name went out came. Sat a long while in the empty room, then left. Told me I was working hard.\"",
"Elder Erwin: (He watches over your shoulder as you read, then turns his head away.)",
"The Niche · Third Canister",
"\"Sixth day. Could not decide. The King of Flame spoke: if we decide, it becomes our sin. Let us ask the scales. If the scales decide, it becomes law. Seven raised their hands. One did not.\"",
"\"The question was written down and sent to the Island of the Scale. The question: one name, and the world. Which is heavier?\"",
"The place where a fourth canister should be is empty. Only the round mark where it stood remains in the dust. Inside the niche, a single line pressed in sealing wax: \"The answer I do not cover. I destroy it. — Velas\"",
"Elder Erwin: There was a man who believed that what is covered is not there. He was wrong. What is covered grows underneath.",
"Ender Golems Guarding the Seat",
"The Eighth Throne",
"The eighth throne is lower than the other seven. There is no crest on its back. It was cut away. The cut is smooth. Done by several hands, with care.",
"An iron lock is set into the middle of the seat. Something looks out from inside the lock. An eye. The fifth eye. The King of Silence made the empty seat his lock.",
"A name was once carved on the armrest. It has been scraped away. Eight grooves remain where the letters were. Only the sixth groove is different. Not scraped but burned. To the width of a finger. Someone touched it with a bare hand.",
"A scrap of grey cloth is caught on the corner of the backrest. The threads were torn downward. It is not from someone who was standing. It is from someone being dragged along the floor.",
"There is a sound behind you. The Elder is on his knees. He tries to rise and his legs will not obey. He is pressing his gloved right hand down with his left. To keep that hand from going toward the throne.",
"Endermen Circling the Empty Seat",
"Shulkers of the Citadel",
"The Elder avoided answering. It's the first time. That he's ever avoided answering me.",
"Gatekeeper of the Empty Throne\nOrdered to bar those who ask. At the last, it pointed to that seat.\nThe eighth seat. A name of eight letters. Not yet written.",
"The Court · The Plaintiffs' Seats",
"A long stone path runs to the middle of the island. Stone benches line both sides. The seats of those who waited for judgment. Every bench shines with the polish of hands.",
"Words scratched into the backs of the benches. \"The neighboring country dammed the river. Third day waiting.\" \"Judgment received. I lost. Even so, it was fair.\" \"The scales do not look at faces. That is why I trust them.\"",
"Archivist Isabel: This was a good place once. Because the scales decided and not a king, even the powerless could win. I'll write it down. This, too, is part of the record of this place.",
"The Court · The Wall of Judgments",
"One wall is covered in judgments. One case to a line. \"The river: to be shared.\" \"The border: to follow the old stones.\" \"The debt: to be repaid, the interest reduced.\" Thousands of lines. The lettering never varies.",
"The very bottom line. \"The question of the eight kings. One name, and the world. Which is heavier?\" In the space for the judgment: \"Does not tip. No judgment. Returned to those who asked.\"",
"Below that the wall changes. The same lettering, but the lines crowd together, overlap, go crooked. \"Weighed again. Does not tip.\" \"Weighed again. Does not tip.\" Without end. At its foot the wall is black with overlapping letters.",
"Archivist Isabel: Because it sent the question back and no answer came. The scales could not close the case. For a thousand years they have been weighing it again, alone.",
"The Court · The Newly Carved Charges",
"Recently carved stone tablets lie scattered at the foot of the scales. They are not judgments. They are charges. \"The crime of running.\" \"The crime of standing.\" \"The crime of walking sunwise.\" \"The crime of moving the hands too much.\" \"The crime of killing.\"",
"Each tablet bears a different date, and they contradict one another. Yesterday running was the crime, and today standing is. Unable to weigh the great question, the scales weigh what they can. Anything at all.",
"On one pan of the scales lie seven seals. The other pan is empty, and yet that empty pan does not rise in the least. There is weight in the empty pan.",
"Archivist Isabel: A name is lying in the empty pan. One our eyes can't see. An erased name. It was erased, and the weight remained. …I think I know why the Elder won't come here. The scales don't look at faces. They won't look at gloves, either.",
"Shulkers of the Void Citadel",
"Here it is. I can see the scales. They're still turning. That long path is the court.",
"The benches. The seats of the people who waited. There's writing on the backs.",
"The whole wall is judgments. Find the bottom line. The last case.",
"There are stone tablets scattered at the foot of the scales. Newly carved. They're not judgments.",
"The Elder is sitting at the end of the bridge. He won't look this way. Not once.",
"There was no judgment. Let's go back and ask the Captain. He's someone who has stood before a thing like that.",
"Captain Roran: I learned it in the inquiry room. If the one asking hasn't settled on the answer, then whatever the one answering does is wrong. So answer only the one thing that's asked.",
"Captain Roran: When the scales post a charge, keep to that one alone. If 'the crime of running' is posted, you don't run. Standing isn't a crime in the meantime. When the next charge is posted, change then.",
"▷ And if the mark of the guilty is put on me?",
"Captain Roran: You get hit harder. That's all. It's no capital crime. The real danger is getting flustered because you're marked and breaking the next charge too. If you got one wrong, stay wrong and keep the next one.",
"Captain Roran: When crystals rise, break them. They're the vessels where the scales store up guilt. Leave them and they burst. The beams of light draw a line on the floor first. Don't step on the line.",
"▷ How did you get through that inquiry, Captain?",
"Captain Roran: I counted heads. Even in front of the examiner. Twelve, one. Twelve, one. …The archivist told me. That I retie my laces not when it's time to leave, but when I remember what I left behind. She's right. That child sees.",
"Golden Apple",
"Geburah, the Scales That Do Not Tip",
"Chapter Four · The Island of the Scale",
"Geburah",
"The case left unclosed for a thousand years",
"Geburah\nThe scales that weighed the quarrels of the eight kingdoms. Trusted because they did not look at faces.\nGiven a question that could not be weighed, they weighed it again for a thousand years.\nLast judgment: let those who asked give the answer.",
"So the scales have stopped.\nThat day I was ordered to guard the door. I did as ordered. That is my charge.",
"Elder Erwin: It was the night of the sixth day that the scales sent back 'no judgment.' The minutes end there. No one wrote down the seventh day.",
"Elder Erwin: …So it stands. In the book.",
"▷ Wasn't there someone taking it all down?",
"Elder Erwin: (He says nothing for a long while.) There was. On the morning of the seventh day he was sent out of the room. On someone's orders. So of that day's business, nothing remains but what could be heard outside the door. And the door was thick.",
"Elder Erwin: Only one thing was heard. The sound of a single chair being pushed back. Someone stood up. After that there was no sound at all. Meaning that not one of the seven said 'sit down.' That was their judgment. Silence.",
"▷ Who was it that stood up?",
"Elder Erwin: The name… (The Elder's mouth moves. No sound comes out. It moves once more.) …I cannot. It is not that I will not. Go. To the Frost Prison. You will hear it there. That child remembers better than I. That child was the youngest there that day.",
"Bram the Smith: Off to the snowfield, are you. Take this. No, it's not a weapon. It's a nail. The nail I pulled from the hundredth peg. Keep it in your pocket. It's no use for anything. Only, isn't it a comfort to have iron in your pocket that held for a thousand years?",
"Bram the Smith: They say the king up there is eighteen. An apprentice's age. You don't put the big hammer in an apprentice's hands. Who put a crown in that child's?",
"Oscar the Fisher: I know a little about being on ice. I walked it fifteen years. I'll say just one thing. If you see something in the ice, don't look at it long. Ice gives back what it has seen. Wearing the face you long to see.",
"Oscar the Fisher: That fellow Morris told me. That I look toward the sea at the end of everything I say. I never knew. It's a habit of thirty years. When you come back, I'll be looking toward the road.",
"Morris the Guide: Uncle Felix drew the snowfield road for you. Here. He meant to come himself and couldn't. He says his feet still won't carry him where there's snow on the ground. He wrote something in the corner of the map in his place.",
]
